        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఠాణా",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఠాణా — ṭhāṇā — \"a police station\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వాళ్ళు దొంగతనం గురించి ఠాణాలో చెప్పారు. vāḷḷu doṅgatanaṁ guriñci ṭhāṇālō ceppāru. They reported the theft at the police station."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An older word for the పోలీసు స్టేషన్; the news still uses it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఠాణా (ṭhāṇā) is a loan from Hindustani thānā, \"a post, a station\", which goes back to Sanskrit sthāna, \"a place\" (CDIAL 13753)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
